// VoxelFluidContract.ush
//
// THE SHARED CONTRACT between the PBF solver (VoxelFluidSim.usf), the
// occupancy/collision volume (VoxelFluidOccupancy/VoxelFluidCollision.ush)
// and, later, the screen-space fluid renderer. Owned by the integrator; the
// solver and collision passes each include this and neither may redefine any
// of it. Change it here or not at all -- two copies of a layout is how the
// water plane once shipped with a stale comment pointing at a constant that
// did not exist.
//
// Part of the water re-architecture (docs/water-rearchitecture-plan-2026-08-09.md):
// particles are PRESENTATION. Nothing in these buffers is ever authoritative
// state -- volumes live in integer ledgers on the CPU. So this file is
// deliberately float-typed and deliberately outside worldgen.ush's digest
// (see VoxelQuadPoolWrite.usf:41-48 for why new kernels stay out of it).

#ifndef VOXEL_FLUID_CONTRACT_USH
#define VOXEL_FLUID_CONTRACT_USH

// ---- units ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Positions and velocities are in UU (1 UU = 1 cm, so one 10 cm voxel = 10 UU),
// world-relative to FluidOriginUU to keep float precision at world scale --
// the world spans tens of km and float UU loses sub-voxel precision past ~1 km,
// which at particle scale is fatal. Every kernel adds/subtracts the origin at
// the boundary, never mid-math.

// Rest spacing: one particle per 10 cm cell at rest density = matches the
// voxel grid, which is what makes despawn-to-fill-units bookkeeping exact:
// one particle == one voxel of water == 255 fill units == 1 L.
#define VOXEL_FLUID_REST_SPACING_UU  10.0f
// Smoothing kernel support radius h. 2.5x spacing is the PBF-standard band
// (Macklin & Mueller use ~2-3x); also the hash grid cell size.
#define VOXEL_FLUID_KERNEL_H_UU      25.0f
// Hard cap the buffers are sized for. The plan's budget math: a 1 m^3/s river
// with ~100 s of visible residence is ~100k sustained; 300k is the ceiling
// the spike must measure, not a target.
#define VOXEL_FLUID_MAX_PARTICLES    (300u * 1024u)

// ---- particle layout ------------------------------------------------------
// AoS, 32 bytes, two float4s -- coalesced pairs, no packing cleverness until
// the spike measures a reason for it.
//   P0: xyz = position UU (origin-relative), w = asuint(flags)
//   P1: xyz = velocity UU/s,                 w = spawn batch id (float)
// Flags (bits of asuint(P0.w)):
#define VOXEL_FLUID_FLAG_ALIVE       (1u << 0)
#define VOXEL_FLUID_FLAG_DESPAWN_BASIN    (1u << 1)  // crossed into a basin extent
#define VOXEL_FLUID_FLAG_DESPAWN_BOUNDARY (1u << 2)  // left the active region
struct FVoxelFluidParticle
{
    float4 P0;
    float4 P1;
};

// The two structured buffers every consumer binds by these names:
//   StructuredBuffer<FVoxelFluidParticle>   Particles       (read passes)
//   RWStructuredBuffer<FVoxelFluidParticle> ParticlesRW     (sim passes)
// plus the live-count buffer:
//   RWStructuredBuffer<uint> ParticleCounts   [0]=alive, [1]=despawnedBasin,
//                                             [2]=despawnedBoundary, [3]=spawnedTotal
// CONSERVATION IS THE TEST: spawnedTotal - despawnedBasin - despawnedBoundary
// == alive, asserted every frame on readback. A counter that cannot prove
// itself is how three false conclusions happened in one session.

// ---- occupancy volume (collision) -----------------------------------------
// 1 bit per 10 cm voxel over the active region, 512^3 bits = 16 MB, packed
// x-major into uints (32 voxels per uint along x). TOROIDAL: the buffer is a
// rolling window, addressed by (local + wrap offset) mod dim -- see item 4.
//   Buffer<uint> / RWBuffer<uint>  FluidOccupancyBits
//   int3  FluidVolumeOriginVoxel     // world voxel coord of LOCAL (0,0,0)
//   uint  FluidVolumeDimVoxels       // 512, and a power of two (the wrap masks)
//   uint3 FluidVolumeWrapOffsetVoxel // STORAGE coord of LOCAL (0,0,0)
// Provided by VoxelFluidCollision.ush (the ONLY file that reads the bits):
//   bool VoxelFluidSolidAtVoxel(int3 worldVoxel);  // outside volume => solid,
//        // so particles can never escape through an unbuilt edge -- the same
//        // "blocked, never guessed" rule the fine tier uses for terrain.
//   float3 VoxelFluidResolveCollision(float3 posUU, float3 prevPosUU);
//        // projects a penetrating particle out along the face normal of the
//        // voxel it entered, killing the normal velocity component.
//
// RATIFIED CLARIFICATIONS (integrator, 2026-08-09, after both sides built):
//  1. FluidOriginUU == FluidVolumeOriginVoxel * 10.0f, always. One origin,
//     computed in one place (FVoxelFluidOccupancyVolume::GetOriginUU); the
//     solver never derives its own. Positions then live in [0, 5120] UU where
//     a float32 ULP is 5 um.
//  2. The SOLVER calls VoxelFluidResolveCollisionEx (same file), not the bare
//     entry point above. The bare form cannot kill normal velocity exactly:
//     PBF derives v = (x - x_prev)/dt, so correcting x alone leaves a residual
//     approach velocity of penetration/dt. Ex returns the contact normal so
//     the solver lifts x_prev onto the same plane. The bare form stays for
//     simple consumers (debug probes).
//  3. The collision walk budget is 16 steps => max supported speed 5,543 UU/s
//     at dt=1/60 (a 157 m waterfall; the plan's named 40 m case needs 2,800).
//     Over budget CLAMPS to the last verified boundary -- water above the
//     supported speed is slowed, never passed through a wall.
//  4. TOROIDAL VOLUME ADDRESSING. **TAKEN 2026-08-09** -- this replaces the
//     "PLANNED, NOT YET CONTRACT" note that stood here, which promised a
//     versioned edit at this spot when the change landed. THE VOLUME IS NO
//     LONGER FLAT. Three spaces, and only the third one changed:
//
//       WORLD    planet voxel coordinates.
//       LOCAL    world - FluidVolumeOriginVoxel, 0..Dim-1. THE GEOMETRIC SPACE
//                and the one everything else in this contract means: particle
//                positions are LOCAL UU (item 1), the boundary box and basin
//                box uniforms are LOCAL UU (items 5, 6), collision projects a
//                particle back onto a LOCAL plane.
//       STORAGE  (LOCAL + FluidVolumeWrapOffsetVoxel) mod Dim -- where the bit
//                lives in the buffer. Used by exactly one expression in
//                VoxelFluidCollision.ush and one in VoxelFluidOccupancy.usf.
//
//     WHAT IT BUYS. Recentring used to rename every bit in the buffer, so it
//     discarded all 16 MiB and refilled 262,144 bricks -- multi-second, water
//     frozen throughout, which is why v0 latched the origin once. Now the bits
//     still in view keep their addresses and only the entering slab is
//     invalidated: 1/8 of the volume per 64-voxel step, marked unbuilt by
//     FluidOccupancyMarkUnbuiltMain and refilled through the existing budgeted
//     UpdateRegion path. The exiting slab is neither cleared nor copied -- the
//     entering slab lands on exactly its addresses.
//
//     WHAT CONSUMERS MUST NOT DO. (a) Do not index the buffer by LOCAL
//     coordinates: every address goes through the wrap. (b) Do not drop the
//     window bounds test on the grounds that the modulo "wraps harmlessly" --
//     the test is on LOCAL and is what keeps outside-is-solid true; without it
//     a voxel one past the west face reads the terrain 51.2 m east. (c) Do not
//     assume FluidVolumeWrapOffsetVoxel is zero, even at startup: it is only
//     zero until the first recentre.
//
//     The offset is the window's ACCUMULATED MOTION mod Dim, not
//     `world mod Dim`. Both are rolling windows; the latter additionally
//     requires a 32-aligned origin or a 32-voxel output word straddles the
//     seam, and the origin is the camera's voxel minus 256. Full argument in
//     voxelcore/fluidoccupancy.h, which is the CPU reference all three
//     implementations mirror and which vxc_tests pins.
//
// RATIFIED, INTEGRATION PASS (2026-08-09, collision + lifecycle wired):
//  5. VOXEL_FLUID_HAS_COLLISION is now 1 in every shipping compile (set by
//     FVoxelFluidShader::ModifyCompilationEnvironment). Consequences of item 1
//     that are now LIVE rather than planned: FluidOriginUU is the occupancy
//     volume's minimum corner, particle positions live in [0, 5120] UU, and
//     the boundary despawn box is therefore NOT origin-centred any more --
//     FluidFinalizeMain tests |p - BoundaryCenterLocalUU| > half extent, with
//     the centre uploaded per frame ((2560,2560,2560) for the flat volume).
//  6. THE BASIN SINK (v1, one basin). FluidFinalizeMain flags an alive
//     particle DESPAWN_BASIN when BasinSinkEnabled != 0 and the particle sits
//     inside [BasinBoxMinLocalUU, BasinBoxMaxLocalUU] with z at or below
//     BasinDatumZLocalUU (the lake's LIVE, ledger-adjusted surface). Counted
//     in ParticleCounts[1]; the CPU credits the scalar ledger at exactly
//     vxc::kFluidLedgerUnitsPerParticle == 255 units per despawn (one
//     particle == one 10 cm voxel == 1 L == 255 WaterCA fill units --
//     derivation and the factor-of-255 test live in
//     voxelcore/fluidlifecycle.h). One basin per frame is a stated v1 limit,
//     not a layout: a table upload replaces the four uniforms when needed.
//  7. VELOCITY AT A WALL. The solver's finalize walks the FULL step (stored
//     position -> constrained position) through VoxelFluidResolveCollisionEx
//     and, when blocked, lifts the stored previous position onto the contact
//     plane before deriving v = (x - x_prev)/dt -- item 2's ratified recipe,
//     now the implementation. Per-iteration DeltaPos correction keeps using
//     the position-only projection; it derives no velocity.
//
// RATIFIED, TOROIDAL PASS (2026-08-09, with item 4):
//  8. PARTICLES ARE REBASED ON RECENTRE; THEY DO NOT BECOME WORLD-ANCHORED.
//     Item 1 ties FluidOriginUU to the window's min corner, so when the window
//     moves, every stored LOCAL position is stale by the delta. The two
//     available answers were "leave positions in world UU and subtract the
//     origin in every pass" and "subtract the delta from every position, once,
//     at the move". The first is not available: the world spans tens of km,
//     a float32 ULP at 30 km is 2 mm, and PBF differences positions at 10 UU
//     spacing -- that is 0.02 % quantisation noise in every neighbour term, and
//     it is the reason item 1 exists.
//
//     So the SECOND. One kernel, FluidRebaseParticlesMain (in
//     VoxelFluidOccupancy.usf, not the solver's file -- recentring is the
//     window's event, and that kernel's header says why), subtracts
//     (newOrigin - oldOrigin) * 10 UU from ParticlesRW[i].P0.xyz over the sim's
//     allocated slots. Velocity is untouched: a frame translation is not a
//     boost. Flags and batch id are untouched.
//
//     WHEN. Between solver ticks, never inside one -- the solver's other
//     position buffers are per-tick transients rebuilt from ParticlesRW, which
//     is exactly why they need no rebase and exactly why this pass must not
//     land mid-tick.
//
//     PRECISION, STATED SO IT IS NOT ASSUMED. The delta is a whole number of
//     voxels, so the shift is an exact multiple of 10 UU (exactly representable
//     out to 2^24 UU = 167 km of motion in one step). p - delta is EXACT
//     whenever the particle moves toward the new origin, and rounds by at most
//     half a ULP at 5120 UU -- 2.4 um, one fortieth of the collision skin --
//     when it moves away. Derivation in voxelcore/fluidoccupancy.h, bound
//     pinned by test_fluidoccupancy.cpp.

#endif // VOXEL_FLUID_CONTRACT_USH
